<title>RUSSIA: Russia's RTS drops 18 shares from first tier.</title>
<headline>Russia's RTS drops 18 shares from first tier.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National brokers' association NAUFOR has decided to transfer 18 shares from its Russian Trading System (RTS) electronic market to the new RTS-2 segment for less liquid stocks, NAUFOR Listing Committee chairman Alexander Kuzetenko said on Monday.</p>
<p>The shares are Aviastar, Baltic Shipping (BMP), Severstal, Elektrosila, FESCO, Karelsky Okatysh, Kirovsky Zavod, Kramz, Novolipetsk Metal, Novosibirsk Metal, Sevkabel, Sameko, Petersburg Port, Bank St Petersburg, Uralelektromed, Uralmash, Verkhnesaldinskoye and Zil.</p>
<p>Kuzetenko said no deals had been recorded in these shares in December or January, although prices had been quoted for them.</p>
<p>He added that NAUFOR had written to members pointing out that shares could also be transferred from RTS-2 to the main RTS, and proposing shares in a series of regional utilities and telecoms, as well as Orenburgneft preferred and Sberbank, should be moved to the full listing.</p>
<p>RTS currently lists 87 shares (including preferred stocks) in 73 companies. RTS-2 lists 72 shares in 47 companies.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
